      "title": "Sexualised, violent threats: female Victorian MPs fear for their safety as they fight more than just next month’s election",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/23/victorian-mps-women-high-alert-safety-state-election-helen-haines-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Hostility from constituents is not new for the state’s politicians, including its premiers. But the alleged attack on Helen Haines has sent a chill down the collective spine</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>On Monday night, Georgie Purcell shared a statement on social media in support of Helen Haines, who earlier that day had been allegedly attacked by a constituent in her regional Victorian electorate.</p><p>Purcell, a Victorian upper house MP whose region partly overlaps with Haines’s federal electorate, wrote that the alleged attack had sent chills down her spine. Being a woman in politics, she said, had changed the way she moved through the world – where she parked her car, which route she took home, even whether she held public events at all.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/23/victorian-mps-women-high-alert-safety-state-election-helen-haines-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-22T14:00:35"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Nunchucks’ wielded by agitated man in Hannah Beazley’s office may have been drumsticks, court told",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/22/hannah-beazley-wa-office-nunchucks-drumsticks-wielded-man-court-hearing-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>John Lawrence Smart charged with being armed in a way that may cause fear but Perth lawyer expresses concern for mental health</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A man accused of making threats <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/22/man-with-nunchucks-arrested-wa-mp-hannah-beazley-ntwnfb\">while armed with “improvised nunchucks”</a> at a Western Australian MP’s electorate office could have been holding a musical instrument, not a weapon, a court has been told.</p><p>John Lawrence Smart appeared on Thursday in the WA magistrates court where his lawyer expressed concern for his mental health. He was not required to enter a plea.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/22/hannah-beazley-wa-office-nunchucks-drumsticks-wielded-man-court-hearing-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-22T12:08:11"
    },
    {
      "title": "Economy set to worsen, with higher unemployment and weaker growth on the way, Jim Chalmers reveals",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/22/jim-chalmers-economy-speech-rising-unemployment-inflation",
      "description": "<p>Treasury is revising all the numbers for the mid-year budget update as economists warn of a difficult six months ahead</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Jim Chalmers has revealed December’s mid-year budget update will project weaker growth and higher unemployment, as economists warn of a difficult six months ahead for the Australian economy.</p><p>Two days after <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/21/odds-of-fifth-interest-rate-hike-this-year-likely-to-shorten-as-rba-deputy-warns-inflation-outlook-worsening\">a senior Reserve Bank official foreshadowed</a> the potential for another interest rate hike in under two weeks’ time, the treasurer in a speech on Friday morning will say “higher inflation is putting people under pressure, tighter monetary policy is weighing on domestic activity, and we can see that in the softening of the labour market”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/22/jim-chalmers-economy-speech-rising-unemployment-inflation\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-22T11:30:43"
    }
